<h2>The Cost Reality of a U-Shape</h2>
<p>A U-shape costs more than an L-shape for the same materials — there is simply more cabinetry (three walls vs two) and two corners to solve instead of one. Here is a realistic estimate for a 14-foot U-shape kitchen (two 5 ft arms + 4 ft base).</p>
